brication adapters were validated against\n# (docs/specs/ are reverse-engineered and version-pinned by design).\n#\n# Daily check → open/update a pinned tracking issue on drift, close it when\n# drift clears. Reporting only, deliberately: this workflow never writes to\n# the repo and never opens a PR.\n#\n# Why not auto-draft the PR (considered and rejected 2026-08-02): CI cannot\n# validate a pin. The probes that earn one need both target CLIs installed, a\n# TTY for the interactive smoke test, and paid model credentials per provider\n# to make the recall turns real. So any PR CI opened would be a mechanical\n# one-line pin bump with nothing behind it — saving a trivial edit while\n# creating a mergeable artifact that asserts a validation nobody performed.\n# An issue cannot be merged; that asymmetry is the whole point. An agent-drafted\n# PR (an earlier idea, needing an ANTHROPIC_API_KEY secret) hits the same wall\n# for the same reason — the key was never the binding constraint.\nname: adapter-drift\non:\n  schedule:\n    - cron: \"17 6 * * *\"\n  workflow_dispatch: {}\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\njobs:\n  check:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    outputs:\n      drift: ${{ steps.drift.outputs.drift }}\n      report: ${{ steps.drift.outputs.report }}\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: 22\n      - id: drift\n        run: node scripts/check-adapter-drift.mjs || [ $? -eq 2 ]\n\n  file-issue:\n    needs: check\n    if: needs.check.outputs.drift == 'true'\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    permissions:\n      issues: write\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/github-script@v7\n        env:\n          REPORT: ${{ needs.check.outputs.report }}\n        with:\n          script: |\n            const title = \"Adapter drift: target CLI released outside validated version range\";\n            const open = await github.rest.issues.listForRepo({\n              ...context.repo, state: \"open\", labels: \"adapter-drift\",\n            });\n            const body = process.env.REPORT +\n              \"\\n\\n_Automated by .github/workflows/adapter-drift.yml — updates daily while drift persists._\";\n            if (open.data.length > 0) {\n              await github.rest.issues.update({\n                ...context.repo, issue_number: open.data[0].number, body,\n              });\n            } else {\n              await github.rest.issues.create({\n                ...context.repo, title, body, labels: [\"adapter-drift\"],\n              });\n            }\n\n  close-issue:\n    needs: check\n    if: needs.check.outputs.drift == 'false'\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    permissions:\n      issues: write\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/github-script@v7\n        with:\n          script: |\n            const open = await github.rest.issues.listForRepo({\n              ...context.repo, state: \"open\", labels: \"adapter-drift\",\n            });\n            for (const issue of open.data) {\n              await github.rest.issues.createComment({\n                ...context.repo, issue_number: issue.number,\n                body: \"Every target CLI's latest release is back inside the adapters' validated version prefixes. Closing automatically.\",\n              });\n              await github.rest.issues.update({\n                ...context.repo, issue_number: issue.number, state: \"closed\",\n              });\n            }\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge/.claude/worktrees/codex-0146-revalidation/.github/workflows/adapter-drift.yml","originalFile":"# Watches the target CLIs' npm releases and flags when they move outside the\n# version prefixes the fabrication adapters were validated against\n# (docs/specs/ are reverse-engineered and version-pinned by design).\n#\n# On drift: opens/updates a pinned tracking issue AND opens a mechanical draft\n# PR that widens the pin and carries the revalidation checklist.\n# When drift clears: closes the tracking issue.\n#\n# The draft PR validates NOTHING, by design. Earning a pin means running the\n# probes, and those need both target CLIs installed, a TTY for the interactive\n# smoke test, and paid model credentials for each provider to make the recall\n# turns real — none of which a runner has. An agent-drafted PR would hit the\n# same wall, so the automation stops at the mechanical edit and a human\n# undrafts after running `npm run smoke:interactive` and the relevant probes.\nname: adapter-drift\non:\n  schedule:\n    - cron: \"17 6 * * *\"\n  workflow_dispatch: {}\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\njobs:\n  check:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    outputs:\n      drift: ${{ steps.drift.outputs.drift }}\n      report: ${{ steps.drift.outputs.report }}\n      branch: ${{ steps.drift.outputs.branch }}\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: 22\n      - id: drift\n        run: node scripts/check-adapter-drift.mjs || [ $? -eq 2 ]\n\n  file-issue:\n    needs: check\n    if: needs.check.outputs.drift == 'true'\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    permissions:\n      issues: write\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/github-script@v7\n        env:\n          REPORT: ${{ needs.check.outputs.report }}\n        with:\n          script: |\n            const title = \"Adapter drift: target CLI released outside validated version range\";\n            const open = await github.rest.issues.listForRepo({\n              ...context.repo, state: \"open\", labels: \"adapter-drift\",\n            });\n            const body = process.env.REPORT +\n              \"\\n\\n_Automated by .github/workflows/adapter-drift.yml — updates daily while drift persists._\";\n            if (open.data.length > 0) {\n              await github.rest.issues.update({\n                ...context.repo, issue_number: open.data[0].number, body,\n              });\n            } else {\n              await github.rest.issues.create({\n                ...context.repo, title, body, labels: [\"adapter-drift\"],\n              });\n            }\n\n  # Mechanical pin widening. One branch per drifted version set, so re-running\n  # daily updates nothing rather than opening a PR a day.\n  draft-pr:\n    needs: check\n    if: needs.check.outputs.drift == 'true' && needs.check.outputs.branch != ''\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    permissions:\n      contents: write\n      pull-requests: write\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: 22\n      - id: existing\n        env:\n          BRANCH: ${{ needs.check.outputs.branch }}\n        run: |\n          if git ls-remote --exit-code --heads origin \"$BRANCH\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n            echo \"exists=true\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n          else\n            echo \"exists=false\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n          fi\n      - if: steps.existing.outputs.exists == 'false'\n        run: node scripts/check-adapter-drift.mjs --fix || [ $? -eq 2 ]\n      - id: commit\n        if: steps.existing.outputs.exists == 'false'\n        env:\n          BRANCH: ${{ needs.check.outputs.branch }}\n        run: |\n          if [ -z \"$(git status --porcelain)\" ]; then\n            echo \"changed=false\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n            echo \"pin is a bare major — widening it is not a one-line change; issue only\"\n            exit 0\n          fi\n          git config user.name \"github-actions[bot]\"\n          git config user.email \"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\"\n          git checkout -b \"$BRANCH\"\n          git commit -am \"Widen adapter version pin for new CLI release (UNVALIDATED)\"\n          git push origin \"$BRANCH\"\n          echo \"changed=true\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n      - if: steps.commit.outputs.changed == 'true'\n        env:\n          BRANCH: ${{ needs.check.outputs.branch }}\n          REPORT: ${{ needs.check.outputs.report }}\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n        run: |\n          printf '%s\\n\\n%s\\n' \\\n            \"$REPORT\" \\\n            \"> Opened as a **draft** by the adapter-drift workflow. The pin edit is mechanical; nothing here has been validated. Run the revalidation steps above locally, record the evidence in the spec's revalidation log, then undraft.\" \\\n            > /tmp/pr-body.md\n          gh pr create --draft --base main --head \"$BRANCH\" \\\n            --title \"Revalidate adapters for new CLI release (draft, unvalidated)\" \\\n            --body-file /tmp/pr-body.md\n\n  close-issue:\n    needs: check\n    if: needs.check.outputs.drift == 'false'\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    permissions:\n      issues: write\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/github-script@v7\n        with:\n          script: |\n            const open = await github.rest.issues.listForRepo({\n              ...context.repo, state: \"open\", labels: \"adapter-drift\",\n            });\n            for (const issue of open.data) {\n              await github.rest.issues.createComment({\n                ...context.repo, issue_number: issue.number,\n                body: \"Every target CLI's latest release is back inside the adapters' validated version prefixes. Closing automatically.\",\n              });\n              await github.rest.issues.update({\n                ...context.repo, issue_number: issue.number, state: \"closed\",\n              });\n            }\n","structuredPatch":[{"lines":[" # version prefixes the fabrication adapters were validated against"," # (docs/specs/ are reverse-engineered and version-pinned by design)."," #","-# On drift: opens/updates a pinned tracking issue AND opens a mechanical draft","-# PR that widens the pin and carries the revalidation checklist.","-# When drift clears: closes the tracking issue.","+# Daily check → open/update a pinned tracking issue on drift, close it when","+# drift clears. Reporting only, delib